Hi Susan,

The  LinComb # returned by backtransform is, I believe, the predicted value on the link scale. In other words, predictions for logit(psi) are 63.2, and 125; and back transformed estimates are the inverse logits of 63.2, and 125...or essentially 1.  Looks like you observed presence at sites 1 and 2 during the first primary period.  Is plot number the same as site number, and is it being entered as a numeric variable (or factor)?

John

