The output from the predict statement gives you what you need:

> > predict(fm, type="psi",newdata=data.frame(habitat=c("Cultivo","Bosque","Inundadas")))

>   Predicted        SE     lower     upper
> 1 0.6788080 0.1251957 0.4068145 0.8668914
> 2 0.6792573 0.1252444 0.4070058 0.8672752
> 3 0.3649530 0.1153894 0.1780297 0.6039362

Then just use your favorite plotting package.  (And I've just used made-up data with the same structure as you have.)

Jim

